  "judgment": {
    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "For q-42886, sec(0)=1, so I is false. Cosine vanishes at 3\\pi/2, giving a vertical asymptote, and sec(2\\pi/3)=-2, so II and III are true. For q-47455, secant's fundamental period is 2\\pi, it decreases on (-\\pi/2,0], and its reciprocal-cosine definition prevents zeros; only III is true. Both answers agree with the earlier selections and their own captured worked solutions. Neither current source solution contains a mathematical error.",
